# The build context of Dockerfile.tinygo alone: BuildKit reads a
# <dockerfile>.dockerignore in preference to the one at the repository root,
# so this can be exact where the root file only subtracts. The spike reads the
# module, the install manifest it fetches the fork with, and one example
# project for the render probe; the announcement's fonts and audio, the docs
# and .git are none of its business.
*
!go.mod
!go.sum
!cmd
!internal
!test
!tools
!scripts
!examples

# The export folder of a release build: output rather than source.
cmd/crier/dist
